LeetCode 3 – Longest Substring Without Repeating Characters
Problem Description

Given a string s, find the length of the longest substring without repeating characters.

A substring is a contiguous sequence of characters within a string.

Approach: Sliding Window + Hash Set

This solution uses the Sliding Window technique with a Hash Set to efficiently track unique characters.

We maintain a window using two pointers:

l: Left pointer representing the start of the window.
r: Right pointer representing the end of the window.

The Hash Set stores the characters currently present in the window.

Whenever a duplicate character is encountered, move the left pointer forward and remove characters from the set until the duplicate is eliminated.

Algorithm
Initialize an empty Hash Set charSet to store unique characters.
Initialize l = 0 as the left pointer and res = 0 to track the maximum length.
Iterate through the string using the right pointer r.
If the current character already exists in the set:
Remove the character at the left pointer from the set.
Move the left pointer one position forward.
Repeat until the duplicate character is removed.
Add the current character to the set.
Update the maximum substring length using r - l + 1.
Return res.


Example

Input:

python
s = "abcabcbb"


Output:

python
3


Explanation:

The longest substring without repeating characters is "abc", which has a length of 3.

Complexity Analysis

Let n be the length of the input string.

Time Complexity: O(n) – Each character is added to and removed from the Hash Set at most once.
Space Complexity: O(min(n, k)) – The Hash Set stores at most the number of distinct characters in the string, where k is the size of the character set.
Key Takeaway

The Sliding Window technique helps solve substring problems efficiently by maintaining a valid window of unique characters.

Using a Hash Set allows constant-time average membership checks, making it possible to solve the problem in linear time without checking every possible substring.
